M03 follow-up: primary objective 1000 (Locate Comm Center) completes on 300,1.
Completing it also sends BASE_ENTERED to the Comm Center (1150002), which
stops M03_Comm_Killed from healing it. On the west (elevator) route, zone
1144502 starts the key conversation M03CON003 and deletes itself in the
same Entered (RMV_Trigger_Zone). The monitor reference goes NULL, so the
end callback that sends 300,1 never runs. Zone 1144502 also marks east
zone 1100005 as entered. If the star then crosses 1100005 before con-yard
zone 1144636, 1100005's RMV_Trigger_Zone sends 900 to 1144636, which
silences M03_ConYardSeen, the last 300,1 sender. In that case 1000 stays
pending for the whole mission at HUD priority 96, above Escape (93). The
Comm Center also stays undamageable, so tertiary 1012 cannot be earned.
The exit itself is not blocked, because it is gated by key 6 from Sakura.

Fallback: when the mainframe is poked (308,1 from terminal 1100009, the
1000 marker object), complete 1000 once if it has not completed yet. The
same star poke sends MCT_ACCESSED (M03_Mct_Poke), so the newly damageable
Comm Center can no longer trigger the mission-fail timer. A later
base-entry 300,1 after the fallback is skipped instead of reannounced. The
state lives in a new saved controller variable (id 13). On the normal
route 300,1 arrives before the poke, so the fallback branch is never taken
and repeated 300,1 events behave as before.

